{
  "id": "data-views",
  "title": "One database, two views",
  "claim": "An owner sees every detail of their own bins and nothing of anyone else's. A researcher gets totals and averages per country, by day or over a period, with names, places and IDs left out.",
  "groups": [
    {
      "label": "Stored",
      "cols": [
        1
      ],
      "tone": "amber"
    },
    {
      "label": "Sorted by",
      "cols": [
        2
      ],
      "tone": "teal"
    },
    {
      "label": "What each view holds",
      "cols": [
        3
      ],
      "tone": "blue"
    },
    {
      "label": "Who sees it",
      "cols": [
        4
      ],
      "tone": "green"
    }
  ],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "db",
      "row": 2,
      "col": 1,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "PostgreSQL",
      "tag": "one database",
      "fields": [
        "users: email, display_name",
        "bins: name, location",
        "*bins: country_code",
        "devices: mac, name",
        "records: timestamp, sensors",
        "bin_events: type, times",
        "ids: user, bin, device"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "scope",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 2,
      "title": "Owner's rows only",
      "sub": "WHERE user_id = me",
      "desc": "others' bins are 404"
    },
    {
      "id": "group",
      "row": 2,
      "col": 2,
      "title": "Group by country",
      "sub": "GROUP BY country_code",
      "desc": "and by UTC day for daily"
    },
    {
      "id": "ownerview",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 3,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Owner view",
      "tag": "dashboard",
      "fields": [
        "bins, devices, alerts // own only",
        "readings // exact time, per device",
        "history // daily averages, up to a year",
        "device keys // shown once"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "researchview",
      "row": 2,
      "col": 3,
      "kind": "record",
      "title": "Research view",
      "tag": "/research/*",
      "fields": [
        "*country_code // the only place kept",
        "day // UTC, or the whole period",
        "bin_count, reading_count",
        "temperature_c, … // avg, min, max, sd",
        "alerts // count and hours to fix",
        "names, emails, locations // removed",
        "MACs and database ids // removed"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "owner",
      "row": 1,
      "col": 4,
      "kind": "actor",
      "title": "Compost owner"
    },
    {
      "id": "researcher",
      "row": 2,
      "col": 4,
      "kind": "actor",
      "title": "Researcher"
    }
  ],
  "edges": [
    {
      "from": "db",
      "to": "scope",
      "label": "their bins",
      "step": 1
    },
    {
      "from": "scope",
      "to": "ownerview",
      "label": "full detail",
      "kind": "data",
      "step": 1
    },
    {
      "from": "ownerview",
      "to": "owner",
      "label": "dashboard",
      "kind": "data"
    },
    {
      "from": "db",
      "to": "group",
      "label": "bins with a country",
      "step": 2,
      "accent": true
    },
    {
      "from": "group",
      "to": "researchview",
      "label": "one row per group",
      "kind": "data",
      "step": 2,
      "accent": true
    },
    {
      "from": "researchview",
      "to": "researcher",
      "label": "key or token",
      "kind": "data",
      "step": 2,
      "accent": true
    }
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Every owner request is answered from the owner's own rows only (`bins.user_id`, `devices.owner_id`). The owner sees exact readings per device, their alerts and their history, and another owner's bin is answered as if it did not exist (404).",
    "The research routes select only the country and aggregates. Bins without a `country_code` are left out. Overall gives one row per country for the chosen period (up to 366 days, 30 by default); Daily gives one row per country per UTC day; Alerts gives a count per country and alert type, with the average hours to resolve. Each sensor comes as its average, minimum, maximum and standard deviation."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Every owner's bins that have a country are included in the research figures. There is no opt-out."
  ],
  "legend": {
    "accent": "the research view",
    "data": "data handed on"
  }
}